{"_meta":{"apiVersion":"16.0.0","changedIn":["5.0.0","3.0.0","2.0.0","1.10.0"],"deprecated":false,"securitySchemes":[{"type":"noauth"}],"since":"1.5.0","status":"stable","version":"3.1.0"},"description":"Builds a monthly budget from a list of expenses at any frequency: normalises everything to a monthly basis, tiers each item (T1 fixed essentials, T2 variable essentials, T3 lifestyle, T4 discretionary), and returns disposable income, savings rate, the biggest optimisable leak and a surplus projection. Use to summarize a household's actual monthly net income and expense items. Ask for the actual expense ledger or item amounts; never fabricate expenses. Entries without a frequency are treated as monthly and disclosed. Omitted investment contributions are treated as zero and disclosed.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"expectedAnnualReturn":{"default":0,"description":"Assumed annual return on invested surplus, percent (default 0).","type":"number"},"expenses":{"description":"Expense items. Known catalogue keys (mortgageRent, groceries, netflix, fuel, ...) are tiered automatically; otherwise pass an explicit tier.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"amount":{"description":"EUR amount. Supply the actual value when applicable; use 0 only when confirmed to be zero.","minimum":0,"type":"number"},"category":{"description":"Optional grouping label (housing, transportation, ...).","type":"string"},"frequency":{"default":"monthly","description":"Payment frequency; everything is normalised to monthly. Default monthly.","enum":["monthly","weekly","quarterly","semiannual","yearly","oneoff"],"type":"string"},"key":{"description":"Catalogue key or free-form label.","type":"string"},"tier":{"description":"Override the automatic tier.","enum":["T1","T2","T3","T4"],"type":"string"}},"required":["key","amount"],"type":"object"},"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"monthlyInvestments":{"description":"Recurring monthly investments/savings, EUR.","minimum":0,"type":"number"},"month